y either — the Instances list, instance overview and Connections pages all read this live. authorizedNetworks (the per-IP allow-list) stays unenforced: Vyomi has no real client IP to match against a simulated instance's allow-list, the same honest limit azure_sql_core.py takes for per-IP SQL firewall rules."]},{"a":[],"id":"gcp.sql.replicas","l":"full","t":"Read replicas","x":["A read replica is a real instance created with masterInstanceName; it mirrors the primary's databases and users — the control-plane metadata this core manages — synchronously on every write, so Replication lag always reads \"0s\" rather than modeling real async replication delay. Table row data (the separate SQL data plane) isn't mirrored, and promoting a replica to a standalone primary (instances.promoteReplica) isn't modeled."]},{"a":[],"id":"gcp.sql.connections-security","l":"limited","t":"Connections: Security (SSL/TLS enforcement, client/server certificates)","x":["A server CA cert is generated for every instance and client certs are real sslCerts.insert/list/delete resources (the private key is returned once, at creation, and never stored again — same as the real API) — but Vyomi issues deterministic, realistic-shaped PEM blobs rather than real X.509/TLS material (no cryptography/OpenSSL dependency, so this loads under Pyodide)."]},{"a":[],"id":"gcp.sql.insights","l":"limited","t":"System insights, Query insights and Cloud SQL Studio","x":["Cloud SQL Studio runs real SQL against the instance's real engine (sqlite3 in Nano, a real Postgres/MySQL in Pro/Max — the SAME engine instances.export/import already drive) and surfaces the engine's own errors; System insights (storage used, active connections, query throughput/error series) and Query insights (recent + top queries with real durations) are derived entirely from that real activity and the real queryLog it writes — never synthetic data."]},{"a":[],"id":"gcp.sql.export-import","l":"limited","t":"Export / import (instances.export, instances.import — SQL and CSV files in Cloud Storage)","x":["Files are written to / read from the simulator's OWN Cloud Storage (a gs:// URI is only parsed, never fetched from Google); a missing bucket or object fails the operation (the Operation carries an error). Each operation completes synchronously."]},{"a":[],"id":"gcp.sql.custom-machine-shapes","l":"limited","t":"Custom machine shapes (db-custom-<vCPU>-<MB>)","x":["vCPU/memory rules are validated like Cloud SQL (1 or even vCPUs up to 96, memory a multiple of 256 MB, 0.9-6.5 GB per vCPU, at least 3840 MB); the shape is stored and billed in the cost model but the database engine is not resource-limited to it."]},{"a":[],"id":"gcp.sql.ssl-mode","l":"limited","t":"SSL/TLS enforcement (sslMode)","x":["sslMode is validated and reported (requireSsl derived); ENCRYPTED_ONLY is enforced on the connection-test path, but client-certificate validation for TRUSTED_CLIENT_CERTIFICATE_REQUIRED is not performed on the wire."]},{"a":[],"id":"gcp.sql.cmek","l":"limited","t":"Customer-managed encryption key (diskEncryptionConfiguration)","x":["The key name shape, same-region rule and existence in Cloud KMS are checked; disk data is not actually encrypted with the key and key disable/destroy does not affect the instance."]},{"a":[],"id":"gcp.sql.backup_restore_clone","l":"limited","t":"Backup runs with data, restoreBackup, clone and point-in-time recovery","x":["Backup runs capture the instance's row data; restoreBackup rewinds data on the same or another same-engine instance; instances.clone copies metadata+data and supports pointInTime via a base snapshot + write log of statements run through the query endpoint (in process memory)."]}],"id":"sql","ops":54,"registry_unreachable":[],"title":"Cloud SQL","total":150}
